{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.985,
   "text": "Something kept digging up my garden at night. So I strapped a trail camera to the old oak in my yard."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.485,
   "end": 15.584,
   "text": "My neighbor, old Mr. Dale, watched from his porch... and gave me one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.184,
   "end": 20.707,
   "text": "If that camera ever takes a picture of you... don't go out to check it."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.807,
   "end": 27.503,
   "text": "For two weeks, it sent photos to my phone every night. Deer. Raccoons. A fox."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.203,
   "end": 31.68,
   "text": "Then, at three-twelve a.m., my phone buzzed."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.88,
   "end": 39.405,
   "text": "It was me. Barefoot. In my pajamas. Standing in the wet grass... staring into the lens."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 40.305,
   "end": 44.849,
   "text": "I don't sleepwalk. And every door was still locked... from the inside."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 45.949,
   "end": 50.024,
   "text": "The next night, another photo. Me again. Closer. Smiling."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 51.324,
   "end": 55.527,
   "text": "So tonight, I sat on my bed in the dark, holding my phone."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 56.227,
   "end": 58.616,
   "text": "At three-twelve... it buzzed."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 60.816,
   "end": 65.36,
   "text": "The photo was of my bedroom window. Taken from the oak tree."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.06,
   "end": 70.647,
   "text": "And sitting on my bed, behind the glass, holding a phone... was me."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.147,
   "end": 76.669,
   "text": "I looked up. Out in the yard, the camera's red light was blinking."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 77.569,
   "end": 82.796,
   "text": "And beside it, in my pajamas, wearing my face... something waved me outside."
  }
 ],
